	// 3D spatial blocking (tiling) for cache locality
	//
	// We split each spatial dimension into blocks:
	//   i -> (I, i), j -> (J, j), k -> (K, k)
	// using into_blocks_dynamic so we correctly handle edge tiles when
	// (n-2) is not a multiple of the tile size.
	//
	// The presence dimensions ('r', 's', 'u') are used internally by
	// Noarr to disable out-of-range iterations in the last (partial) tile.
	// When used through traverser.order(...), the states passed to our
	// lambdas still use the original indices ('i', 'j', 'k'), so we can
	// write the stencil exactly as before.
